{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790963584,"nonce":"38pz1nKiBQmFVYV1jIpnZStj53A=","title":"Std.parseInt returns its null sentinel as an Int","message":"Row: Issue9198.\n\n`Std.parseInt` maps `returns: primitive =\u003e I64` (stdlib/runtime_mapping.rs) and\n`haxe_std_parse_int` returns `i64::MIN` for \"not a number\". Nothing turns that back into null:\n`var r = Std.parseInt(\"axolotl\")` boxes MIN as a real Int, so `r == null` is false and `\"\" + r`\nprints -9223372036854775808. `eq(null, r)` passes only because unboxing truncates MIN to 0.\n\n```haxe\nvar r = Std.parseInt(\"axolotl\");\nSys.println(r == null);   // true\nSys.println(\"r = \" + r);  // r = null\n```\n\nHazard: a Null\u003cInt\u003e expectation converts to Ptr(U8); casting the raw I64 to a pointer there lost\nTestXML before (see bugs_dynamic_member_dispatch_by_name, round 2).","files":null}]}